From fcff60a8473374c31bf9d36b11b04565e414d93a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:44:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Access Point mode: tune the sockets, count the clients, name
 the mode

The GT-BE19000 tester's write-up and diag arrived 2026-09-13. The fact the
report did not state is the one that explains it: that box is in Access Point
mode (sw_mode=3). Three of the four items are not port defects at all - they
are Reaper surfaces that quietly assume a routing box, in code every model
shares. A fourth came out of the same capture.

rc/firewall.c - start_firewall() returns at !is_routing_enabled() long before
the block that raises net.core.rmem_max/wmem_max to 16 MB and
netdev_max_backlog to 4096, so an AP, repeater or media-bridge box ran on the
stock 212992 ceiling no matter how often the firewall was restarted. The
capture shows exactly that: rmem_max 524288 and backlog 1000 after three
restart_firewall calls, which caps any stream whose tool calls
setsockopt(SO_RCVBUF) - the Ookla engine included. The three writes move into
reaper_socket_ceilings() and the non-routing return calls it on the way out.
These are not firewall state and had no reason to sit behind that guard.
Routing mode still takes the call in the same place in the body; its behaviour
is unchanged.

www/Main_ReaperDash.asp - two surfaces, one cause. The client tiles polled
get_clientlist() and dropped every row failing isOnline!=='1'; networkmap
derives that flag from the DHCP leases and conntrack, and a bridging box has
neither (the capture: 0 and 0), so the dashboard showed 0 clients while 16
stations were associated and the Devices page listed them all. In a
non-routing mode the tiles now read reaper_dev.cgi, which builds presence from
the wl assoclists, the bridge FDB and the ARP table and carries the band the
tiles bucket on - folding MLO links and AiMesh nodes the way the Devices page
does. It polls at 30 s rather than 10: action=status popen()s wl per radio,
VIF and station, which is why the Devices page reads it on demand.
The Internet card derived its verdict from wan0_state_t, structurally 0 with
no WAN of its own, and painted a healthy router red. It now names the
operation mode in a neutral colour, and the live poll - whose "fast while it
is down" cadence would otherwise run a 4-second request for the life of the
page against a state that cannot change - is not started at all.

others/reaper_diag 12c (v1.3.17) - rtrafd, gkd and rchqd are all started
behind !is_routing_enabled(), and rtrafd accounts off conntrack, which a
bridging box never populates. "rtrafd is enabled but not running" was
therefore a false WARN on the tester's box. svc() now reports the designed
idle state for the mode instead, the same correction rmcpd's line already
carries. Only sw_mode 2 and 3 flip it: an unreadable sw_mode keeps the
louder behaviour rather than silencing a real fault.

Scoped to the operation mode rather than to the model, at the owner's call:
a routing box - which is every other reporter and every default install -
behaves exactly as before, and a box of any model later switched to AP mode
is fixed too.

Not addressed here: the duplicate menu entries after opening UPnP, which
still wants a screenshot and the tester's add-on list.

make mk-rc BUILD_NAME=RT-BE96U exit 0, no new warnings. hiddencheck PASS,
csrfcheck 0 breakers over 60 request sites, static_checks 13/13 (dict
lockstep 6921 - no new tokens), sh -n and busybox sh -n clean on the diag,
all six inline script blocks parse. New host test
build-scripts/tests/test_apmode_surfaces.py compiles reaper_socket_ceilings()
out of the real source and asserts the values it writes, then asserts every
non-routing path is present; it fails against the pre-fix tree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
